# Bedrock-Patch: 0004-bedrock-outgoing-header-floor
# Area: integration
# Upstream-Paths: services/network/url_loader.cc
# Reason: phase 7 — makes privacy/network/request_headers real. URLLoader::ScheduleStart
#   is the last point before net::URLRequest::Start(), and the only place where the
#   referrer Chromium computed and the assembled request headers both exist; it also
#   runs again for each redirect, which is a new request to a new host.
#   The patch collects the referrer, the target, the top-level document and the
#   names of the headers already present, asks bedrock::integration::DecideHeaders,
#   and applies exactly what comes back: SetReferrer for a shortened referrer,
#   RemoveRequestHeaderByName for each refused client hint. It carries no policy —
#   the floor lives in src_overrides/bedrock/privacy/network/request_headers.* and
#   the seam is host-tested by network_hook_test.
#   Direction is one-way by construction: the decision may only shorten what
#   Chromium was going to send, never lengthen it (invariant 85).
# Owner: integration
# Chromium-Version: 151.0.7922.173
# Upstream-Bug: none
# Drop-When: Chromium grows a supported per-request referrer/client-hint policy
#   hook, or the header floor moves behind the same profile plumbing that will
#   carry per-site shields into the network service.
diff --git a/services/network/url_loader.cc b/services/network/url_loader.cc
index 98f6f203cd..8aeeb6edb6 100644
--- a/services/network/url_loader.cc
+++ b/services/network/url_loader.cc
@@ -4,6 +4,9 @@
 
